{
  "program": "CBSTM03B",
  "caseId": "case08",
  "description": "End of file on XREFFILE, then CLOSE. One row is seeded; the second READ reports '10' and returns the area unchanged, and the CLOSE that follows reports '00'. The pair matters because it proves the two statuses come from the same XREFFILE-STATUS area (app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL:87-89) rather than from a shared one: a '10' left over from the end of file would be visible in the CLOSE's LK-M03B-RC if 2900-EXIT moved anything other than that file's own status.",
